From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/qcom-mpm: tell RPM there is no wakeup timer in s2idle

The vMPM region starts with two words that hold the time at which the
APSS wants to be woken, as a 64-bit arch timer value, ahead of the
enable, edge, polarity and status registers. The driver skips them, so
they stay 0, a wakeup that is already due.

On a Redmi 4 Prime (msm8953) every RPM master (APSS, MPSS, PRONTO and
LPASS) voted XO off through a 60 s s2idle, yet the RPM sleep stats show
no XO shutdown at all. The vendor kernel writes the next timer event
there, and for system suspend "no timer" (all ones).

Do the same in s2idle, where only wakeup interrupts, routed through the
MPM, end the sleep. Keep writing 0 outside s2idle: RPM can't see the
CPUs' timers, and with XO shut down nothing would fire them.

---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-qcom-mpm.c
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
 #include <linux/slab.h>
 #include <linux/soc/qcom/irq.h>
 #include <linux/spinlock.h>
+#include <linux/suspend.h>
 
 /*
  * This is the driver for Qualcomm MPM (MSM Power Manager) interrupt controller,
@@ -292,6 +293,20 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The two words in front of the registers hold the time at which the
+ * APSS wants to be woken, in arch timer ticks. RPM shuts XO down only
+ * when that time is far enough away.
+ */
+static void qcom_mpm_write_wakeup(struct qcom_mpm_priv *priv, u64 ticks)
+{
+	writel_relaxed(lower_32_bits(ticks), priv->base);
+	writel_relaxed(upper_32_bits(ticks), priv->base + 4);
+
+	/* Ensure the writes are completed */
+	wmb();
+}
+
 static int mpm_pd_power_off(struct generic_pm_domain *genpd)
 {
 	struct qcom_mpm_priv *priv = container_of(genpd, struct qcom_mpm_priv,
@@ -301,6 +316,14 @@
 	for (i = 0; i < priv->reg_stride; i++)
 		qcom_mpm_write(priv, MPM_REG_STATUS, i, 0);
 
+	/*
+	 * In s2idle only a wakeup interrupt ends the sleep, and those come
+	 * through the MPM, so there is no timer for RPM to keep. Outside it,
+	 * leave the wakeup time at 0: RPM can't see the CPUs' timers, and with
+	 * XO shut down nothing else would fire them.
+	 */
+	qcom_mpm_write_wakeup(priv, idle_should_enter_s2idle() ? U64_MAX : 0);
+
 	/* Notify RPM to write vMPM into HW */
 	ret = mbox_send_message(priv->mbox_chan, NULL);
 	if (ret < 0)
